        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I understand the reason for voice activity to fade up the icon during mute, this change of mic icon behaviour has made me mute/unmute far more than I used to so I can actually even tell if my mic is on or off. At the very least the option should be there to revert back to the previous behaviour if people choose to do so. I absolutely hated this change and every single person I spoke to about it hates it too. Hell I was so annoyed by it that I felt I had to provide feedback here for the first time in all my years on VRC.\n\nEven an inversion of the current behaviour would make more logical sense; when mute you don't need to see the icon light up but when unmuted you should. From a safety point of view surely we deserve to know if our voice is actually being transmitted? If these changes are in aid of preventing screen burn-in, why not make that a separate sub-setting for people to choose between? Not everyone has a Bigscreen Beyond.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
